     1	# WhipNode Onboarding Spec - the three-rung ladder
     2	
     3	Status: v2, panel-reviewed. Synthesized from two adversarial design panels
     4	(2026-08-19: init-flow, trial-ladder; three cross-vendor seats each,
     5	grounded in this repo), then the draft was itself reviewed by a third
     6	three-seat panel whose findings (2 blocker verdicts) are folded in below.
     7	Decisions are panel-adjudicated; open parameters are marked OWNER-CALL.
     8	Do not widen scope during implementation without re-review.
     9	
    10	## Goal
    11	
    12	Zero-to-first-capture in under 30 seconds for an agentic-CLI user, with no
    13	shipped credentials, no unattended use of anyone's identity, abuse cost
    14	bounded by a fixed daily budget, and an honest upgrade lane:
    15	
    16	```
    17	RUNG 0  zero-click anonymous trial      ~10 captures/day, no email, <30s
    18	RUNG 1  claim (wall-triggered) OR whipnode init  -> free account, 50/day
    19	RUNG 2  pro (existing pricing page)
    20	```
    21	
    22	Rung 0 complements `whipnode init`; it never replaces it. Every rung is
    23	independently kill-switchable without touching the rungs above it.
    24	
    25	## Threat rule that shapes everything below
    26	
    27	**Anything printed into agent/CLI/IDE output is assumed leaked** (agent
    28	transcripts, logs, screenshots). Therefore: no raw keys and no
    29	capability URLs ever appear in MCP tool text; claim links are inert
    30	locators; conversion requires possession of the trial key. Residual risk,
    31	stated honestly: **theft of the 0600 credential file grants claim
    32	authority over that trial** - blast radius is capped by never-merge, zero
    33	pre-claim identity, and 24h item TTL. If credential-file theft is observed
    34	in practice, the recorded escalation path is the codex-seat dissent: an
    35	Ed25519 installation keypair with loopback signing, so the possession
    36	secret never exists in any file an agent can read.
    37	
    38	## Prerequisite bugfixes (live gaps today; ship before or with rung 0)
    39	
    40	1. **capture.ts skips the per-IP limiter.** `handleCapture` checks only
    41	   the account daily quota (capture.ts:233-237); `checkUploadRateLimit`
    42	   (rate-limit.ts:16-58) is never called on the capture path. Apply it to
    43	   capture for **trial and free plans** (paid plans exempt or
    44	   plan-scaled - the 20/IP/hour budget would throttle a 1000/day pro
    45	   account and NAT'd teams).
    46	2. **MCP path loses the client IP.** The internal Request forged in
    47	   mcp.ts (~:1008) drops `CF-Connecting-IP`; forward the original client
    48	   IP explicitly so IP-scoped checks see it.
    49	3. **Rate limiter fail-opens.** rate-limit.ts:20-21 returns
    50	   `allowed: true` on missing IP. Add a `failClosed` option; trial-plan
    51	   requests always set it (no IP -> no trial issuance, no trial capture).
    52	4. **PLAN_LIMITS fallback hole.** rate-limit.ts:70 falls back
    53	   `PLAN_LIMITS[plan] ?? PLAN_LIMITS.free` - an omitted `trial` entry
    54	   silently grants 50/day. Add `trial` to `AccountPlan` (types.ts:32) and
    55	   `PLAN_LIMITS` (constants.ts) **in the same PR as the migration**, and
    56	   audit every plan-union switch/guard/display for the new value.
    57	
    58	## Rung 0 - anonymous trial
    59	
    60	### Issuance (on `initialize` only)
    61	
    62	Trigger: unauthenticated MCP `initialize` **mediated by the `npx
    63	whipnode` CLI wrapper**, when `FEATURE_ENABLE_ANON_TRIAL=true`. Two
    64	transport realities (panel-verified):
    65	
    66	- The worker rejects unauthenticated MCP before parsing today
    67	  (mcp.ts:291-293); issuance is a carve-out for `initialize` only.
    68	- **The raw `wn_` key never travels in JSON-RPC/tool text.** A vanilla
    69	  remote-MCP client has no way to persist an in-band key anyway. The key
    70	  is delivered once in a response header consumed by the `npx whipnode`
    71	  stdio wrapper, which writes the 0600 credential file and thereafter
    72	  supplies `X-API-Key`. Bare HTTP-MCP clients without the wrapper get the
    73	  existing `-32000` plus one line: run `npx whipnode init`.
    74	- Reconnects authenticate with the stored key; they never mint a second
    75	  trial (the 1/IP/24h cap also blocks accidental remints).
    76	
    77	Gate (ALL, in order, fail-closed):
    78	- `CF-Connecting-IP` present.
    79	- Cloudflare bot-management score >= `BOT_SCORE_MIN` (env, default 30,
    80	  OWNER-CALL) ; deny-list of hosting/datacenter ASNs (documented env
    81	  list - neither exists in-repo today, both must be built).
    82	- Per-IP-hash issuance cap: 1 trial / 24h (reuse `hashIp`).
    83	- Global issuance counter under cap (see Spend ceiling).
    84	
    85	On pass: create `accounts` row (`plan='trial'`, `email=NULL` - migration
    86	makes email nullable; SQLite UNIQUE permits multiple NULLs, no
    87	sentinels), one `wn_` key, enroll the `mcp_devices` row via the existing
    88	mcp.ts:333-367 path.
    89	
    90	### Trial shape (`PLAN_LIMITS.trial` + enforcement inventory)
    91	
    92	| Dimension | Trial value |
    93	|---|---|
    94	| Items (captures+uploads)/day | 10 (OWNER-CALL; codex-seat dissent: 3 until billing telemetry) |
    95	| Viewports per capture | 1; `full_page`, `4k`, `1080p` rejected in capture validation |
    96	| Retention (TTL) | 24h |
    97	| Concurrent processing | <= 2 (reservation/release, not just a constant) |
    98	| API keys / devices | 1 / 1 (account-level check) |
    99	| OCR + prompt packs | included (it is the product) |
   100	| Unclaimed account expiry | 7 days - a NEW cleanup.ts task: revoke the key (existing cascade revokes devices, api-keys.ts:139-142), then delete the account row; a PENDING claim freezes this expiry |
   101	
   102	Enforcement is not `PLAN_LIMITS` alone: capture-option validation,
   103	account-level device quota, and concurrency reservation each need
   104	explicit code paths.
   105	
   106	### Spend ceiling (the control that makes rung 0 survivable)
   107	
   108	Table: `trial_counters (day TEXT PRIMARY KEY, issuances INTEGER NOT NULL
   109	DEFAULT 0, captures INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0)` - UTC-day keyed,
   110	append-only (never reset in place; the day key IS the reset, matching the
   111	00:00 UTC wall copy). Every increment is atomic-conditional immediately
   112	before allocation:
   113	
   114	    UPDATE trial_counters SET captures = captures + 1
   115	      WHERE day = ? AND captures < ?    -- meta.changes == 0 -> 429
   116	
   117	Start caps ~250 issuances / 200-500 captures per day; alert email at 80%.
   118	Cap-exhaustion 429 of legitimate onboarding is ACCEPTED fail-closed
   119	behavior - the ceiling converts worst-case abuse from an unbounded
   120	Cloudflare Browser bill into a chosen number; per-IP caps alone lose to
   121	residential proxies.
   122	
   123	### Kill switch
   124	
   125	`FEATURE_ENABLE_ANON_TRIAL=false` stops new issuance only. Live trial
   126	keys hit the wall copy; claimed (`free`/`pro`) accounts are never touched
   127	by any rung-0 control.
   128	
   129	## Rung 1a - the claim flow (wall-triggered)
   130	
   131	### The wall response (what the agent relays)
   132	
   133	Any trial wall returns error text the agent relays verbatim. **It
   134	contains a command, not a link** - no claim_id, no capability URL:
   135	
   136	    Trial limit reached (10/10 today; resets 00:00 UTC). I cannot raise
   137	    this. Ask your human to run: npx whipnode claim - that keeps this
   138	    workspace, key, and history, and unlocks 50 captures/day free.
   139	    Or start fresh with: npx whipnode init. Details: whipnode.com/claim
   140	
   141	(`whipnode.com/claim` is the static docs page. Per-claim locators exist
   142	only after a human runs the command, and even then are consent-only -
   143	see below.)
   144	
   145	### The claim protocol
   146	
   147	Roles: browser Authorize = **consent only**. Trial-key-authenticated CLI
   148	poll = **the conversion**. A leaked locator or a phished click can
   149	therefore never convert anything by itself.
   150	
   151	1. Human runs `npx whipnode claim`. TTY required - documented as a UX
   152	   guard, not a security control (agents can PTY); the security is the
   153	   key-possession + code-match design. Claim-start authenticates with
   154	   the trial key (key must be `status='active'`); it invalidates any
   155	   prior pending claim for this account (one pending claim per trial;
   156	   concurrent starts can't race two emails).
   157	2. Claim-start snapshots the trial's recent capture hosts
   158	   (`{host, created_at}` x3, parsed at claim time - there is no
   159	   `captured_url` column; items carry the URL only in `note`) onto the
   160	   pairing row. CLI prints an 8-char code **on the TTY only** (redacted
   161	   from any log output) and opens `whipnode.com/claim/<claim_id>`
   162	   (random locator, single-use, **10-min TTL**, no credential).
   163	3. Page: Turnstile (OWNER-CALL: day-one vs adaptive) -> email form ->
   164	   magic link with a **claim-specific token purpose**. The existing
   165	   verify handler MUST NOT run for claim tokens - today it upserts an
   166	   account by email and 302s to /dashboard (auth-verify.ts:38-77), which
   167	   would both violate never-merge and strand the flow. Claim-verify
   168	   instead: prove the mailbox, write `verified_email` onto the pairing
   169	   row, create no account, redirect to the approve page.
   170	4. Approve page shows: the snapshot hosts + times ("only authorize if
   171	   these are yours"; empty snapshot renders "0 captures - only approve
   172	   if you just started this trial"), device name + created-at, free-tier
   173	   bullets, and an input where the human **types the 8-char code from
   174	   their terminal** (typed, not displayed - defeats phishing direction
   175	   (b): an attacker's page can't show a code that matches your TTY).
   176	   One Authorize button; nothing pre-checked.
   177	5. **Existing-email rule: never merge.** If `verified_email` matches an
   178	   account other than this trial: refuse ("This email already has
   179	   WhipNode - run whipnode init on that account"), consume the claim_id,
   180	   allow a fresh `whipnode claim` with a different email (rate-limited
   181	   per trial account). The email-existence oracle is accepted;
   182	   magic-link send stays neutral.
   183	6. Authorize marks the pairing `approved` (atomic, single-use,
   184	   auth-verify.ts:22 consume pattern). **No account mutation here.**
   185	7. The CLI poll (authenticated with the trial key) finds `approved` and
   186	   executes the conversion as one atomic UPDATE whose WHERE re-asserts:
   187	   pairing approved + unconsumed, account `plan='trial'`, key + device
   188	   still `active`, email still unclaimed. Sets `email`, `plan='free'`.
   189	   Same key, same `mcp_devices` rows, items intact - the agent's config
   190	   never breaks at the upsell moment. Any assertion fails -> 409
   191	   "Trial expired - run npx whipnode init", no mutation.
   192	
   193	## Rung 1b - `whipnode init` (the deliberate path)
   194	
   195	As adopted by the init panel: `npx whipnode init` -> email -> magic link
   196	(claim/init-purpose token: verify writes `verified_email` to the pairing
   197	row, creates the account only at Authorize - not the /dashboard upsert
   198	path) -> approve page ("Authorize this device", the one consent click) ->
   199	key delivered once on the **POST** poll -> 0600 file -> auto
   200	`claude mcp add` when present -> smoke capture. 10-min pairing TTL.
   201	
   202	OWNER-CALL (recorded as UNRESOLVED init-panel dissent, not adopted): raw
   203	API key vs per-device session token as what init delivers. Whichever is
   204	chosen, init and rung-0 issuance must follow the same choice.
   205	
   206	## Shared pairing table (init + claim compose here - get this right)
   207	
   208	One table, two state machines, discriminated:
   209	
   210	    device_codes (
   211	      id, kind TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(kind IN ('init','claim')),
   212	      code_hash,            -- locator/user-code hashes, never plaintext
   213	      user_code_hash,       -- claim: the typed 8-char code
   214	      verifier_hash,        -- init: PKCE-style verifier binding
   215	      account_id,           -- claim: the trial account; init: NULL until Authorize
   216	      device_name, verified_email,
   217	      activity_snapshot,    -- claim: JSON {host,created_at}[]
   218	      status CHECK(status IN ('pending','verified','approved','consumed','denied','expired')),
   219	      created_at, approved_at, consumed_at, expires_at  -- 10 min both kinds
   220	    )
   221	
   222	Poll is **POST** (verifier/key in body/header, never query-string logs).
   223	Auth differs by kind: init poll = verifier; claim poll = trial API key.
   224	**Only the init poll may ever return key material**; the claim poll
   225	returns status and executes conversion. Every transition is a
   226	conditional atomic UPDATE.
   227	
   228	## Rung 2 - pro
   229	
   230	Unchanged. Upsell surfaces (honest walls only): limit-hit errors name the
   231	plan + pricing URL; expired-item fetch names Pro retention; >25MB / 2nd
   232	key / extra viewports name the exact Pro row; `whipnode_status` prints
   233	plan + N/limit + pricing URL; prompt-pack footers carry attribution +
   234	expiry only, quota line only when <20% remains. No recurring ads.
   235	
   236	**Free-tier shape - OWNER-CALLs recorded by the init panel, not silently
   237	resolved:** quota (grok: keep 50/day status quo - default; codex:
   238	100/month + 10/day), viewport cap on free (codex: 1/request; grok: max
   239	2/call; today free gets all 6), devices (both: tighten to 3/account from
   240	10/key). Defaults ship as: 50/day, viewports unchanged, 3 devices -
   241	change via constants, not code.
   242	
   243	## Endpoint + client inventory
   244	
   245	Worker: trial issuance inside unauthenticated `initialize`;
   246	`POST /auth/device/start` (kind-aware); `POST /auth/device/poll`;
   247	`POST /auth/device/approve` (session-authed, kind-aware); claim/init
   248	magic-token purpose in auth-magic-link/auth-verify; `GET /claim/:id`
   249	page; capture validation for trial options; trial cleanup task.
   250	
   251	CLI (`npx whipnode`, stdio MCP wrapper + subcommands): `init`, `claim`,
   252	`status`; TTY checks (UX guard); 0600 credential file; key printed never
   253	(delivered via header/poll and written straight to file).
   254	
   255	## Data + privacy posture
   256	
   257	Pre-claim accounts store: hashed IP, derived device name, captured page
   258	bytes (24h), activity snapshot on an open claim. No email, no name.
   259	Public copy: "no account, no email required" - NOT "no data".
   260	Post-claim adds exactly: verified email. 90-day device session expiry;
   261	revocation cascades key -> devices (existing behavior).
   262	
   263	## Decision log
   264	
   265	- Zero-click trial: APPROVED by the trial-ladder panel (reopened from the
   266	  init panel's consent constraint on a new fact: pre-claim accounts hold
   267	  no identity, so account-creation consent has no subject; consent
   268	  remains for email attach - the Authorize click + typed code).
   269	- Bearer links/keys in agent surfaces: REJECTED unanimously, twice - the
   270	  wall copy is command-only, and conversion happens on the
   271	  key-authenticated poll, not in the browser.
   272	- Spec v1 -> v2 (review-panel findings applied): conversion moved from
   273	  Authorize to poll; claim-specific magic-token purpose; kind
   274	  discriminator + full state machine on device_codes; rung-0 key via CLI
   275	  wrapper header only; revoked-mid-flow assertions; UTC-day atomic
   276	  counters; PLAN_LIMITS fallback closed; IP limiter scoped to
   277	  trial/free; 10-min TTLs everywhere; typed code replaces displayed
   278	  code; activity snapshot at claim-start; email-oracle accepted;
   279	  free-tier dissents restored as OWNER-CALLs.
